# SEC-0028 — the production runner may invoke the compose broker and nothing else.
# The broker validates its own arguments: the service must be in a compiled-in
# allowlist and the sha must already be reachable from origin/main. Widening this
# line, or adding a second entry, re-opens the escalation this exists to close.
ci-runner ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/local/sbin/arcanada-compose-broker
# INFRA-0417: on arcana-prd the deploy runner is a SEPARATE account. That host
# carries six runners under one `ci-runner`, two of which (arcana-prd-general,
# arcana-prd-db) advertise the `docker` label and accept jobs with `services:`
# — so that account must keep the docker group, while a deploy runner must not
# have it. The split mirrors how arcana-prod solved the same collision.
#
# This line already existed on the host and NOT in git, which is the exact
# failure the previous commit to this file had to repair. Returning it here
# means a reinstall from the repository no longer silently removes the only
# account that can deploy on that machine.
ci-runner-deploy ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/local/sbin/arcanada-compose-broker
